        "    if (s.equals(\"a\")) list.remove(s);",
        "}"
      ],
      "options": [
        "list becomes [b, c]",
        "ConcurrentModificationException",
        "list stays [a, b, c]",
        "compile error"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Structurally modifying a list during for-each fails fast on the next iterator step. (Trivia: removing the second-to-last element sneaks through — that's why this removes the first.) Use an Iterator or removeIf.",
